  "program": {
    "source": "const A=3,C=1,K=0.5,R=0.14,S=2,N=64,MAXS=40,LIM=10,ST=[0.6,1.7],AS=2;\nconst loss=(x,z)=>0.5*(A*x*x+C*z*z);\nconst rand=n=>{const s=Math.sin(n*91.345+17.17)*24634.6345;return s-Math.floor(s);};\nconst gauss=n=>Math.sqrt(-2*Math.log(Math.max(1e-9,rand(n))))*Math.cos(2*Math.PI*rand(n+0.5));\nconst sd=B=>S*Math.sqrt(Math.max(0,N-B)/((N-1)*B));\nfunction grad(s,inp,noisy){const e=noisy?sd(Number(inp.batchSize)):0,k=s.run*1009+s.step*2+1;return[A*s.x+e*gauss(k),C*s.z+e*gauss(k+0.37)];}\nconst over=s=>s.dead||s.step>=MAXS;\nfunction advance(s,inp){if(over(s))return s;const g=grad(s,inp,true),lr=inp.learningRate,x=s.x-lr*g[0],z=s.z-lr*g[1];return{...s,x,z,step:s.step+1,dead:loss(x,z)>LIM,path:s.path.concat([[x,z]])};}\nconst fresh=(run,kept)=>({x:ST[0],z:ST[1],step:0,run,dead:false,path:[ST],kept});\nexport function initialState(){return fresh(0,[]);}\nexport function reduce({state:s,event:e,inputs}){\nif(e.type==='step')return advance(s,inputs);\nif(e.type==='action'&&e.action==='newRun')return fresh(s.run+1,s.step>0?s.path:s.kept);\nreturn s;}\nconst cl=v=>Math.max(-2,Math.min(2,v));\nconst lift=p=>[cl(p[0]),K*Math.min(loss(p[0],p[1]),8)+0.05,cl(p[1])];\nfunction aim(dx,dz,show){const l=Math.hypot(dx,dz),h=Math.SQRT1_2;return show&&l>1e-6?{visible:true,quaternion:[dz/l*h,0,-dx/l*h,h],scale:[1,l*AS,1]}:{visible:false};}\nexport function evaluate({inputs,state}){\nconst s=state||initialState(),L=loss(s.x,s.z),live=!over(s),lr=inputs.learningRate;\nconst g=grad(s,inputs,true),t=grad(s,inputs,false),dx=-lr*g[0],dz=-lr*g[1];\nconst p=lift([s.x,s.z]);\nreturn{nodes:{\nball:{position:[p[0],p[1]-0.05+R,p[2]]},\nstepArrow:aim(dx,dz,live),\ntrueArrow:aim(-lr*t[0],-lr*t[1],live&&inputs.showTrueGradient),\ntrail:{points:s.path.map(lift)},\nghost:{points:s.kept.map(lift)}},\nreadouts:{steps:s.step,loss:L,stepLen:live?Math.hypot(dx,dz):0,status:s.dead?'diverged':live?'running':'finished'}};}\n"
  },
  "assumptions": [
    "Illustration: a made-up two-setting loss bowl with simulated batch noise, not a real model trained on real data.",
    "Loss = (3x² + z²)/2, drawn at half height. Along x, plain steps overshoot when the learning rate is above 1/3 and swings grow above 2/3. At 1 the run diverges within a few steps.",
    "Noise: each slope part gets added Gaussian noise with SD 2·√((64−B)/(63·B)). That is 2 at batch 1 and exactly 0 at batch 64. The noise is centred on the true slope.",
    "Arrows: the orange one is the next step, −learning rate × noisy slope. The grey one is −learning rate × true slope. Both are drawn at 2× their true length and hidden once a run ends.",
    "Each host step is one update. Use 0.25× speed to follow it. A run ends after 40 steps, or as diverged once the loss passes 10.",
    "Noise comes from a fixed seed: Reset replays run 0. 'New run, keep last path' uses the next noise values and keeps the finished path as the ghost.",
    "Ball and paths outside the drawn square are shown at its edge, with heights capped. The Loss readout keeps the true value."
  ]
}